# Test: an l2tp pool the reload removes leaves show system dns.
# Initial config: the observer plugin and an l2tp block whose ipv4 pool
#   writes dns-primary 203.0.113.53 and no dns-source, so the pool's
#   built-in list applies.
# After SIGHUP: the observer plugin and the environment block alone; the
#   l2tp root is gone, so the engine removes the l2tp-pool plugin (its only
#   config root is l2tp) while the daemon runs.
# Expected: show system dns lists the l2tp-pool selection at
#   "l2tp pool ipv4 dns-source" before the reload, and after it still
#   answers the router's selection (consumer system) but no l2tp-pool
#   consumer at all.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-home-cpe-23b review round 3 ISSUE 3: the pool plugin's
#   OnBye handler (internal/component/l2tp/plugins/pool/register.go) sends
#   its withdrawal while the engine removes the plugin, inside the removal
#   grace, and the registry forgets the consumer. The pool unit test in
#   publish_test.go calls withdraw() directly, so it proves neither
#   the wiring nor that the emit is read during removal.
# PREVENTS: a removed pool plugin whose last selections show system dns and
#   ze doctor keep reporting until the daemon restarts.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: break overlay rwinv/c23b-withdraw-pool/
#   (poolInstance.withdraw() taken out of the OnBye handler): the registry
#   keeps the l2tp-pool consumer and its last selection after the reload
#   removed the plugin. Observed red (rwinv/out-gb15/b15-withdraw-pool.log:46):
#   "the removed l2tp-pool is still listed with 1 selection(s)". The poll also
#   requires the system consumer's "system dns-source" selection, which
#   proves the answer it judged came from a live registry, not an empty one.
#
# Sequencing: the observer writes observer.initial-ok once the pool is
#   listed; the trigger waits for it, copies config2.conf over ze-bgp.conf,
#   sends SIGHUP and writes reload.done, after which the observer polls for
#   the withdrawal.
#
# No cmd= line carries `:timeout=`: a foreground command's timeout replaces
# option=timeout as the budget of the whole test.

option=env:var=ze.l2tp.skip-kernel-probe:value=true
option=env:var=TEST_SECRET:value=s3cr3t
option=timeout:value=60s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external show-system-dns-withdraw-pool-test {
		run "le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw-pool"
		encoder json
	}
}
l2tp {
	enabled true
	shared-secret s3cr3t
	pool {
		ipv4 {
			gateway 10.99.8.1
			start 10.99.8.10
			end 10.99.8.20
			dns-primary 203.0.113.53
		}
	}
}
environment {
	l2tp {
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1
			port $PORT
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
plugin {
	external show-system-dns-withdraw-pool-test {
		run "le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw-pool"
		encoder json
	}
}
environment {
	l2tp {
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1
			port $PORT
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show system dns lists the l2tp pool's default list before the reload
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show system dns drops the removed l2tp pool and keeps the router selection
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
